{"tool_name":"qubic","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"qubic","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/QUBIC","license":"CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0","summary":"The core function of this R package is to provide the implementation of the well-cited and well-reviewed QUBIC algorithm, aiming to deliver an effective and efficient biclustering capability. This package also includes the following related functions: (i) a qualitative representation of the input gene expression data, through a well-designed discretization way considering the underlying data property, which can be directly used in other biclustering programs; (ii) visualization of identified biclusters using heatmap in support of overall expression pattern analysis; (iii) bicluster-based co-expression network elucidation and visualization, where different correlation coefficient scores between a pair of genes are provided; and (iv) a generalize output format of biclusters and corresponding network can be freely downloaded so that a user can easily do following comprehensive functional enrichment analysis (e.g. DAVID) and advanced network visualization (e.g. Cytoscape).","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:00:49Z","last_update_date":"2026-08-30T02:28:29.398651Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.40.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:qubic","credit":[{"name":"Qin Ma","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Yu Zhang","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/QUBIC"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Gene expression clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0313"}]}],"name":"QUBIC","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw635"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene expression","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0203"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"QUBIC","home":"https://bio.tools/qubic","license":"CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0","version":"1.40.0","summary":"The core function of this R package is to provide the implementation of the well-cited and well-reviewed QUBIC algorithm, aiming to deliver an effective and efficient biclustering capability. This package also includes the following related functions: (i) a qualitative representation of the input gene expression data, through a well-designed discretization way considering the underlying data property, which can be directly used in other biclustering programs; (ii) visualization of identified biclusters using heatmap in support of overall expression pattern analysis; (iii) bicluster-based co-expression network elucidation and visualization, where different correlation coefficient scores between a pair of genes are provided; and (iv) a generalize output format of biclusters and corresponding network can be freely downloaded so that a user can easily do following comprehensive functional enrichment analysis (e.g. DAVID) and advanced network visualization (e.g. Cytoscape).","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:qubic:1.2.1/cmd/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":25,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2025"},{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":2,"year":"2020"},{"count":2,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2023"},{"count":7,"year":"2018"},{"count":8,"year":"2019"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw635","pmid":"28172469","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"QUBIC: a bioconductor package for qualitative biclustering analysis of gene